---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import ProjectHero from '../../../../components/ProjectHero.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const trail = [
  { slug: 'murakami', title: 'MURAKAMI MAMBO !!', path: `${base}en/murakami/` },
  { slug: 'jte', title: 'Japanese Traditional Events', path: `${base}en/murakami/jte/` },
];

const OFFICIAL = 'http://jte.ryumurakami.com/';
---

<Layout
  title="Japanese Traditional Events (JTE) — Ryu Murakami | Japonéson"
  description="Ryu Murakami's bilingual book Japanese Traditional Events, eight years in the making, with a CD of Japanese songs supervised by his close friend Ryuichi Sakamoto."
  lang="en"
>
  <Header lang="en" />
  <main>
    <ProjectHero
      kicker="RYU MURAKAMI · 2016"
      title="Japanese Traditional Events"
      subtitle="Respect & Love — eight years in the making."
      image={`${base}images/murakami/jte_hero.jpg`}
      imageAlt="The framed garden of Hōsen-in, a temple in Ohara, Kyoto — a bamboo grove and young maples seen across a red felt mat from the empty tatami room. Photographed by Shoko Shiraishi, April 2022."
      align="center"
      height={720}
      fit="cover"
      overlayTop={0.15}
      overlayBottom={0.35}
    />

    <div class="container breadcrumb-wrap">
      <Breadcrumb trail={trail} lang="en" />
    </div>

    <section class="essay">
      <div class="essay-inner">
        <p>This book came into my hands in January 2024.</p>
        <p>
          It was published on 4 July 2016, but it says inside that it took about
          eight years to finish.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ryu Murakami, it seems, began it after seeing a film about the Japanese
          American internment camps of the Second World War, and the book is written
          in both Japanese and English.
        </p>
        <p>
          It comes with a CD of Japanese nursery songs and <em>shōka</em> (school
          songs), supervised by Ryuichi Sakamoto. The two were close friends —
          Murakami often wrote in his essays that he would meet Sakamoto in New York
          and then travel on to Cuba by way of Cancún. It seems he consulted him
          about Cuban music as well.
        </p>
        <p>
          Knowing that this CD came after Murakami's stories of America and Cuba, and
          that Sakamoto fell ill with cancer while the book was still being made,
          moved me deeply. The music is quiet, warm and beautiful. You can hear
          Sakamoto's feeling for a dear "friend" turned into sound.
        </p>
        <p>
          The book is out of print now, but the special site tells you why it was
          made and lets you listen to the music. Do pay it a visit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <section class="quote-block">
      <div class="quote-inner">
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            There was a moment during the making of JTE when it dawned on me, with
            all the clarity of a fine sunrise, that my attitude toward Japanese
            traditional events was basically one of <strong>“respect and love.”</strong>
            Normally I might feel a bit self-conscious about using such words, but in
            this case they felt so natural and right that I found myself embracing
            them as our subtitle.
          </p>
          <footer>
            — Ryu Murakami, from the <a href={OFFICIAL} rel="noopener">official JTE site</a>
          </footer>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="book">
      <div class="book-inner">
        <figure class="book-photo">
          <img
            src={`${base}images/murakami/jte_book.jpg`}
            alt="A copy of Japanese Traditional Events (JTE) standing on a wooden stand at Shoko Shiraishi's home, with plum branches arranged in a Hagi-ware vase above it. Photographed January 2024."
            width="750"
            height="1000"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>Photographed by Shoko Shiraishi, January 2024.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <dl class="credits">
          <div><dt>Title</dt><dd>日本の伝統行事 — <em>Japanese Traditional Events</em> (JTE)</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Subtitle</dt><dd>大切に思うこと、愛すること — <em>Respect &amp; Love</em></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Text</dt><dd>Ryu Murakami</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Illustrations</dt><dd>Yuka Hamano</dd></div>
          <div><dt>English translation</dt><dd>Ralph McCarthy</dd></div>
          <div>
            <dt>Music</dt>
            <dd>
              <em>Japanese Children’s Songs and Shōka</em>, supervised by Ryuichi Sakamoto —
              three CDs (Japanese, English, and karaoke)
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div><dt>Cover</dt><dd>Haruka Ayase (nail art: Haruna Takahashi)</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Publisher</dt><dd>Kodansha, 4 July 2016 · ISBN 978-4-06-219960-5</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <p class="official">
          <a href={OFFICIAL} rel="noopener">→ The official site for <em>Japanese Traditional Events</em></a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer lang="en" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .breadcrumb-wrap { padding-top: 1rem; padding-bottom: 0; }

  .rule {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 1rem auto 0;
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .essay { padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 1rem; }
  .essay-inner { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .essay-inner p {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #2a2a2a;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .pending {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .quote-block { padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem; }
  .quote-inner { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .quote-block blockquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 1.4rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .quote-block blockquote p {
    font-family: var(--font-italic-quote);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #444;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .quote-block footer {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .quote-block footer a { color: var(--color-accent); }

  .book { padding: 1rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
  .book-inner {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 300px 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .book-photo { margin: 0; }
  .book-photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .book-photo figcaption {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .credits { margin: 0; }
  .credits > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07);
  }
  .credits dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display-cinzel);
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .credits dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #2a2a2a;
  }

  .official {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display-cinzel);
    font-size: 17px;
  }
  .official a { color: var(--color-accent); }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .book-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .book-photo { max-width: 300px; }
    .credits > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.2rem; }
  }
</style>
